186503331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503636 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f00c5744-2f0c-56be-b32e-366a3f1f09f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1089 #edb/ref 17592186503648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503646 #edb/ref 1090 #uuid "8dcaf9fe-4b85-5cb3-9d12-8cc51f2110ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186503762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186503793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186503795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186503796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186503809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186503823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186503837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186503838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1085 "Mary and her little brother Sam live together. Their house is located $960$ meters from the community park. The following graph shows Mary's distance from home as she walks home from the park.\n\n![](images/73/733489f3198f4b26719b2ad770eae3d965f8f008f4a8171ae67c837af68436e0.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1086 #uuid "0193adbb-a9ed-50c0-8c39-bfe4319c7952" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503648 #edb/ref 1087 #edb/ref 17592186503795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503665 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503665 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503665 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503665 #edb/ref 1071 "How long did it take Sam to reach the community park from home? Express your answer as a fraction or a decimal.\n\nIt took Sam$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$minutes to reach the community park" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503665 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1f3496f7-56e0-5008-8c00-9a987ff3c119" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503665 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the community park is $960$ meters from Sam's home, we need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{300}{11}t=960.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply both sides of the equation by $11$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{300}{11}t & =960 \\\\ 11\\cdot \\frac{300}{11}t & =11\\cdot 960 \\\\ \\cancel{11}\\cdot \\frac{300}{\\cancel{11}}t & =11\\cdot 960 \\\\ 300t & =11\\cdot 960\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $300$ to isolate $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}300t & =11\\cdot 960 \\\\ \\frac{300t}{300} & =\\frac{11\\cdot 960}{300} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{300}t}{\\cancel{300}} & =\\frac{11\\cdot 960}{300} \\\\ t & =\\frac{11\\cdot 16\\cdot \\cancel{60}}{5\\cdot \\cancel{60}} \\\\ t & =\\frac{11\\cdot 16}{5} \\\\ t & =\\frac{176}{5}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it took $\\frac{176}{5}=35\\frac{1}{5}$ minutes for Sam to reach the community park." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503674 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503674 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503674 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166758" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503674 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503674 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ba/ba84a222a38abb930dbf0dde24479abcbfb3ccdca4f50beec0792e90e212d0b0.png)\n\nSam left home to go to the community park at the same time that Mary left the community park to go home. Both Mary's and Sam's distances from home are shown in the graph above. Based on the graph, we conclude that:\n\nMary and Sam met$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$minutes since they both started moving.\n\nThey met at a distance of$\\,$ \n{{field-2}}$\\,$meters from their home." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503674 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31feda6f-3ad0-51f3-97d6-60332a952f6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503674 #edb/ref 1074 "Mary and Sam meet when they are at the same distance from home. At this moment, their graphs intersect.\n\n![](images/8a/8afd4e9a8374ebe1e35200f6172e7fac9ef6c132d84e532c3ac44c25cb838a0d.png)\n\nIn this case, we have the point $(11,300).$ So, Mary and her brother met $11$ minutes since they started moving at a distance of $300\\,\\text{m}$ away from their home." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503691 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503691 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166756" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503691 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503691 #edb/ref 1071 "The road between Mary's home and the community park is straight. What is the distance between Mary's home and the point halfway between Mary's home and the community park?\n\nThe distance between Mary's home and the halfway point is$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$meters." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503691 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5a6b0d11-b6de-598d-ac31-b89f5088f71e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503691 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/d0/d06fbf44c15301b9fc764823eb6d51652d9fe9426b5aa01b764e4b409d9dc6d5.png)\n\n \n\nLet $H$ be Mary's home (located at $x=0\\,\\text{m}$) and let $P$ be the community park (located at $x=960\\,\\text{m}.$)\n\nTo find the number ${x}_{m}$ corresponding to the midpoint $M$ between Mary's home and the community park, we use the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+960}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{960}{2} \\\\  & =480.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/8b/8bba4fb81dc0a1e303a1f2bbe5e9d02fe159dfac83f29153401a2e7fda0b8df0.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the point that lies halfway between Mary's home and the community park is $480\\,\\text{m}$ from Mary's house." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503692 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503692 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503692 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503692 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the data from part $5,$ find an **exact** equation of the line for the distance $d$ covered by Sam after $t$ minutes.\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503692 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d896b5e-5f76-50d5-9895-9e0c9b778976" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503692 #edb/ref 1074 "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $d=mt+b.$ So we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $d$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $d$-axis at the origin. So, the $d$-intercept is $b=0.$\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,0)$ and $(11,300),$ so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{d}_{2}-{d}_{1}}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{300-0}{11-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{300}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=\\frac{300}{11}$ and the $d$-intercept $b=0$ into the slope-intercept form $d=mt+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\nd=\\frac{300}{11}t\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503722 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503722 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166757" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503722 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503722 #edb/ref 1071 "The equation that describes Mary's distance from home is $d=960-60t.$ Hence, Mary reaches the midpoint $M$ after$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$ minutes." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503722 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a524e974-5d6b-572b-94df-d3f5d29063a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503722 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the midpoint is located at $d=480$, we need to solve $960-60t=480.$\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $960$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}960-60t & =480 \\\\ 960-60t-960 & =480-960 \\\\ -60t+0 & =-480 \\\\ -60t & =-480\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-60:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-60t & =-480 \\\\ \\frac{-60t}{-60} & =\\frac{-480}{-60} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-60}t}{\\cancel{-60}} & =8 \\\\ t & =8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mary reaches the halfway point after $8$ minutes." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503726 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503726 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166755" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503726 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503726 #edb/ref 1071 "Mary covered a distance of $960$ meters in $16$ minutes. Then, Mary's speed was{{field-1}} meters per minute." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503726 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a8749a36-d229-5422-be78-2c6cc7c08abc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503726 #edb/ref 1074 "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in meters per minute, we divide the number of meters, $960,$ by the number of minutes, $16.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{960}{16} & =\\frac{960÷8}{16÷8} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{2} \\\\  & =120÷2 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mary's speed was $60$ meters per minute." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503744 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503744 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166754" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503744 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503744 #edb/ref 1071 "The slope of the line is $m\\,=\\,${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503744 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d59c0884-c058-5785-9ee6-42436f91acb4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503744 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that the line passes through the points $(0,960)$ and $(16,0).$ So, we let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,960)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(16,0),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-960}{16-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-960}{16} \\\\  & =-60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line is $m=-60.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503753 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503753 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186503554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503753 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503753 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503753 #edb/ref 1071 "Mary wonders where and when they'd meet if Sam left home $3.8$ minutes earlier and walked with a speed of $50$ meters per minute. She finds that the distance $d$ from home they'd meet can be modeled using the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}d+60t=960 \\\\ d-50t=190.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time (in minutes) since Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$minutes after Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet at a distance of $\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,$meters from home." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503753 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee041a5d-3530-58d3-9ad7-acdf10ca4984" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503753 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve the given system of linear equations, we will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the second equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $d$ adding to both sides of the equation $50t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d-50t=190 \\\\ d=190+50t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $d$ with $190+50t$ in the first equation and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d+60t=960 \\\\ (190+50t)+60t & =960 \\\\ 190+110t & =960 \\\\ 110t & =960-190 \\\\ 110t & =770 \\\\ t & =\\frac{770}{110} \\\\ t & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they would have met after $t=7$ minutes.\n\nIf we substitute $t=7$ into $d=190+50t$, we can find the value of $d:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =190+50t \\\\  & =190+50(7) \\\\  & =540\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they meet at a distance of $540$ meters from home." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503762 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186503823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503762 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0bdd0386-927d-558d-9807-930f47803e99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503762 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503792 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5dd1df4f-567d-5267-ad8e-a2abbf17fd85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503792 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503793 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "69cd4aee-1950-50d7-9c94-0376b1dce32f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503793 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503795 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186503809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503795 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "72162a7a-4fa7-5951-9274-5e2f648f9c73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503795 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503796 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186503762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503796 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7368ec56-83d3-5cdc-934b-1e058dae67da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503796 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503809 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186503796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503809 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "90df7b35-08f9-5219-955a-9347410e43e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503809 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503823 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186503837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503823 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c6764a5f-7aec-5ca9-a463-76d8b24f9533" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503823 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503837 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186503838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503837 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f1478ad7-0bdd-5a21-a700-d1940b5cc0f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503837 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503838 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186503793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503838 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f706ef77-3c61-5f5d-a5ef-2c7d49458de6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186503838 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503665 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
